{
  "name": "manatee",
  "_about": "THE MANATEE (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/bigmam/manatee.py, built from scratch on the cetaceans' plan): a West Indian manatee (sea cow), 3 m -- FAT and spindle-round, broader than deep, the rough grey-brown skin mottled; a small earless head on a short thick neck hardly set off; the big SQUARE BRISTLY MUZZLE, its front a flat pad tilted down, the split upper lip two fat pads thick with short stiff bristles (whisker strands), the nostrils two valves on top of the snout's tip, tiny eyes; short paddle FLIPPERS hanging forward and down, three pale NAILS at the tip; no dorsal fin; the big ROUND PADDLE tail, one flat disc. Pale propeller scars across the back. Coats: grey, brown, algae-green. A slow swimmer (`fly`); its paddle beats up and down. Written whole by its script.",
